# Coloured glass by its thickness (Beer and Lambert; docs/apps/raytrace.md, "Example scenes"): three
# panes of the same glass, 5, 15 and 45 hundredths thick, and three balls of another that take
# its light the sooner, densities 0.5, 2 and 8. The light is behind them: their shadows are coloured.
camera target 0 0.3 0.3 turn 0 tilt 32 far 4.2 lens 0.6
background colour 1 1 1 power 0.15
object Ground plane scale 5 colour 0.85 0.85 0.85
object "Thin pane" box kind glass density 4 colour 0.25 0.6 0.95 size 0.7 0.7 0.05 place -1.05 0.35 -0.4
object "Pane" box kind glass density 4 colour 0.25 0.6 0.95 size 0.7 0.7 0.15 place 0 0.35 -0.4
object "Thick pane" box kind glass density 4 colour 0.25 0.6 0.95 size 0.7 0.7 0.45 place 1.05 0.35 -0.4
object "Light ball" ball kind glass density 0.5 colour 0.9 0.35 0.1 scale 0.5 place -0.8 0.25 1
object "Ball" ball kind glass density 2 colour 0.9 0.35 0.1 scale 0.5 place 0 0.25 1
object "Dense ball" ball kind glass density 8 colour 0.9 0.35 0.1 scale 0.5 place 0.8 0.25 1
light Light place 0 4 -3 radius 0.3 power 140
